      "effect": "combination",
      "trigger": "proactive-hardening",
      "sb_only": true,
      "touches_mac_sb": false,
      "summary": "Lookup to mach services with the WebKit extension should list the allowed services (WebContent sandbox)",
      "subject": "Lookup to mach services with the WebKit extension should list the allowed services",
      "description": "Lookup to mach services with the WebKit extension should list the allowed services\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=203619\n\nReviewed by Alexey Proskuryakov.\n\nTo tighten the mach lookup rule which allows lookup to services with the \"com.apple.webkit.extension.mach\"\nextension, all allowed services should be listed. Currently, we are only creating mach lookup extensions to\n\"com.apple.iphone.axserver-systemwide\", but more will come in the future.\n\nNo new tests. Testing this requires UI interaction on the device to enable Accessibility.\n\n* Resources/SandboxProfiles/ios/com.apple.WebKit.WebContent.sb:\n\n\nCanonical link: https://commits.webkit.org/217014@main\ngit-svn-id: https://svn.webkit.org/repository/webkit/trunk@251821 268f45cc-cd09-0410-ab3c-d52691b4dbfc",
      "profiles": [
        "WebContent"
      ],
      "resources": [
        "mach-lookup"
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "rules": [
        "com.apple.iphone.axserver-systemwide",
        "com.apple.webkit.extension.mach"
      ],
      "files": [
        "Source/WebKit/Resources/SandboxProfiles/ios/com.apple.WebKit.WebContent.sb"
      ],
      "lines_added": 4,
      "lines_deleted": 1,
      "allow_added": 3,
